# Story page: gale
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = Gale Cliffs
---
Nearly at the top of the world, the wind began to argue with {name} about where it was going.

On Gale Cliffs a gust could pick up a whole snake and set it down a little to the left, as a nanny might move a toddler away from a stove.

In a hollow out of the wind lay a red stone that pulled at apples the way a moon pulls at tides. {name} carried it with great satisfaction, and lunch came to it.
